# Secrets. Nothing matching these may ever be committed.
# Every credential this vault uses lands in one of these patterns.
credentials/
credentials.json
*.json.key
.env
.env.*

# Per-vault identity. Never shared between vaults.
vault.config.json

# Permissions granted on this machine by clicking "always allow". Machine-local
# by nature, and not something to carry to another laptop unreviewed.
.claude/settings.local.json

# The shared system. It is its own repository, cloned into System/ and updated
# from there, so this repository must not try to track a second copy of it.
System/

# macOS noise
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*

# Obsidian per-machine state
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/cache

# Build and run artefacts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
logs/*
# ...except the trend record, which is the point of running maintenance at all.
!logs/metrics.csv
*.tmp
*.log

# Photos, recordings and video that arrive in the Inbox, usually sent from a
# phone. A picture of a letter and a dictated voice note are among the most
# personal things this vault ever holds, and git history is permanent: once
# pushed, a file cannot be taken back out. They stay on this machine.
#
# The cost is real and deliberate. These are the one thing in the vault with no
# backup, so a dead disk loses them. Anything worth keeping should be read,
# written into a note, and the note is what survives.
#
# Documents are not covered on purpose: a PDF is usually a record worth backing
# up. Add the extension here if that turns out to be wrong.
Ideaverse/Inbox/*.oga
Ideaverse/Inbox/*.ogg
Ideaverse/Inbox/*.opus
Ideaverse/Inbox/*.m4a
Ideaverse/Inbox/*.mp3
Ideaverse/Inbox/*.wav
Ideaverse/Inbox/*.jpg
Ideaverse/Inbox/*.jpeg
Ideaverse/Inbox/*.png
Ideaverse/Inbox/*.heic
Ideaverse/Inbox/*.gif
Ideaverse/Inbox/*.webp
Ideaverse/Inbox/*.mp4
Ideaverse/Inbox/*.mov
Ideaverse/Inbox/*.webm
